Z||000005||skitime||10-29-2001||09:14 PM||||Hey,  Kempo they look cool. For the digital camera keep checking Circuit City for a returned one.  They will give an 3 year warranty on it for about $40.  SO I paid $89 for a $250 camera and an extra $40 to have the warranty extended to 3 years. Seemed like a deal and I love the camera.  It was an Olympus D360L.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||kempo||10-29-2001||09:23 PM||||Yes, Enkei RSF2 17x7 with 40offset.  These rims are very sweet and will look pretty damn good on a fiero, imo!  Also, they are pretty light weight, about 10 lbs. a wheel.  I also want to say thanks to everybody who helped me out with the wheel and tire questions that I've had!  Think I'll be going with BF Goodrich 225/45-17 Z rated.  Any suggestions?<P>Thanks for the advice, skitime!  Your pics are real nice and high quality!<P>Monkeyman- these boxes are so sweet!  They are virtually weightless and held together very well!  I could jump on these boxes without them caving in, or out, or whatever!  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||artherd||10-30-2001||05:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by kempo:<BR><B>Think I'll be going with BF Goodrich 225/45-17 Z rated.  Any suggestions?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, go with 215/45/17 front, and 235/40 (or 45)/17 rear.  You'll love it long time.<P>Enjoy the 17s, Fieros love them!!!<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000008||onfire||10-30-2001||05:39 AM||||What artherd said. 215's on the front 235's on the rear.<P>I have 215 40's on mine. On all four corners. My next set of tires on the rear will be wider. <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresigtoo.jpg"> ||||reg||1
